12.5 Empirical Strategy
We estimate the following fixed effects panel regression model: \[
\text{Growth}_{it}
= \beta \cdot \text{GovExp}_{it}
+ \alpha_i
+ \gamma_t
+ \varepsilon_{it}
\] where: - ( _i ) are country fixed effects - ( _t ) are year fixed effects Standard errors are clustered at the country level. This specification controls for time-invariant country characteristics (such as geography, institutions, or long-run development levels) as well as common global shocks affecting all countries in a given year.
